### Unknown keys on the Usage page  {% id="unknown-keys" %}

The [Usage page](https://aistudio.google.com/usage) in Google AI Studio groups
requests it can't match to a named API key in the project under
**(unknown keys)**. This includes keys deleted more than 30 days ago, keys
without a display name, and requests made with other credentials, such as OAuth.

## Creating keys in the Google Cloud console  {% id="cloud-console" %}

{% tab label="Windows" %}
  1. Search for "Environment Variables" in the Windows search bar.
  2. Click **Environment Variables** in the System Properties dialog.
  3. Under **User variables** or **System variables**, click **New...**.
  4. Set the variable name to `GEMINI_API_KEY` and the value to your API key.
  5. Click **OK** to save. Open a new terminal session to load the variable.

{% /tab %}

